# Dyscover Implementation Plan

Goal: Build "Dyscover," a gamified React Native (Expo) app for dyslexia literacy, integrating Duolingo-style UI and Google Gemini AI for handwriting analysis.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Firebase Credentials:** I will initialize Firebase, but please verify if you have an existing Firebase project or if I should set it up with placeholder credentials for now.
> - **Gemini API Key:** The Gemini AI integration will require a valid API key. Ensure this key is stored securely (e.g., in `.env` or EXPO environment variables).

## Proposed Changes

We will start with an Expo project setup using Expo Router.

### Project Scaffolding
- Initialize project with `npx create-expo-app@latest .`
- Install `lucide-react-native`, `firebase`, `@google/generative-ai`.
- Configure Expo router and bare minimum structure.

### Theme Configuration
#### [NEW] src/styles/theme.ts
- Define colors: Primary Cream `#FFFDD0`, and UI colors for nodes and text.
- Define typography: Bold sans-serif fonts with 1.5x letter spacing.

### State & Logic
#### [NEW] src/context/UserContext.tsx
- Implement a React Context to manage:
  - Hearts (max 5)
  - XP (score)
  - Streak
- Logic to deduct hearts and track progress.

#### [NEW] src/services/firebase.ts
- Initialize Firebase app.
- Setup Firestore integration to save and load User XP and Streak.

#### [NEW] src/services/gemini.ts
- Integrate `@google/generative-ai` to use `gemini-1.5-flash`.
- Provide a prompt that enforces simple encouraging JSON output for analyzing handwriting images (base64) for b/d reversals and spacing issues.

### Components
#### [NEW] src/components/Header.tsx
- Displays current Streak (🔥), Hearts (❤️), and XP (🏆).

#### [NEW] src/components/LearningNode.tsx
- A single circular node for the learning map.

### Screens
#### [NEW] app/index.tsx (Home Screen)
- Acts as the main "Learning Map".
- A ScrollView displaying the Header and a winding path of 10 `LearningNode` components.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None specified currently; can be expanded if needed.

### Manual Verification
- We will start the Expo web preview using `npx expo start -w`.
- Verify the header tracks correctly.
- Verify the Learning Map renders 10 nodes in a scrolling path geometry.
- Stub the Gemini and Firebase calls initially to confirm UI behavior before full end-to-end testing.
